Package: prokrustes
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}
Recommends: llama.cpp-tools
Description: fill text templates with grammar-constrained model output
 prokrustes fills a text template whose placeholders each carry a Python
 regular expression. Each pattern is compiled to a GBNF grammar that is
 handed to a llama-server, so every generated value is guaranteed to match
 its pattern. Output is parsed back against the template and re-checked,
 and only the filled document is printed.
 .
 Chat mode (via the server's /apply-template endpoint) is on by default,
 servers on Unix domain sockets are supported, and an optional <think>
 reasoning block lets the model reason before emitting the document.
